title: "The Sunday Drive"
date: "2026-07-30"
excerpt: "On the last Sunday in July, at eleven-oh-eight in the morning, a seventy-four-year-old retired elementary-school librarian named Nancy Wickham Ackerman pulls out of the small gravel lot behind First Presbyterian on Jackson Street in Millersburg, Ohio, in a dark green 2004 Buick Century with ninety-one thousand miles on it, and turns left onto Walnut — the first turn of a thirty-eight-minute loop through her town she has driven every Sunday since the memorial for her husband Dale in the March of 2020. Along the loop, at nine unremarkable places, she thinks about eleven organizations. Somewhere on the second floor of a converted mill in a small county-seat town two hours east, on the same Sunday morning, the record for Nancy W. Ackerman in the development file of the one organization she gives to most reads *sustaining $85 since 2011, mail only, no engagement noted, do not upgrade*. A short letter, with a great deal of affection, on the small green Buick that is a working portfolio of a life — and the twenty years of software that has never once asked to ride shotgun."
tag: "Field Notes"
